      ],
      "text": "**I’d limit your time outdoors today in Kuala Lumpur, especially exercise—but you may not need to stay inside all day.** A citywide hourly estimate reported **poor PM2.5 at 9 a.m. today, October 16**, while readings can vary by neighborhood and hour. ([pollution-alert.com](https://pollution-alert.com/en/malaysia/pollution/geo-1735161/kuala-lumpur?utm_source=openai))\n\nWith asthma, choose indoor activity if you can; if you go out, keep exertion light and carry your reliever inhaler. Check Malaysia’s DOE air-quality readings for your area before heading out, and follow your asthma action plan. Air pollution can trigger asthma symptoms. ([eqms.doe.gov.my](https://eqms.doe.gov.my/apims/main?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you’re wheezing or short of breath and your reliever isn’t helping, seek urgent medical care.",
